### 1.4 Colour usage rules

- Keep the interface **clean, minimal and spacious**.
- Use **Royal Blue for primary interactions** and important actions (one primary button per view).
- Use **Navy to establish brand identity** and hierarchy: logo, headings, navbar, hero, footer, admin sidebar.
- Use **white and soft grey** to keep text readable; cards sit on `#F7F9FC` with a `#E8EDF4` border and a very soft shadow.
- **Reserve Automotive Red** for promotions, discounts, "Hot deal" / "Price drop" badges and key highlights. Do not use it for ordinary buttons or navigation.
- Use the **status colours consistently** everywhere (same colour means the same thing on the website and the dashboard).
- Keep colours **identical across the public website and admin dashboard**.
- **WhatsApp green** (`#25D366`, the official WhatsApp brand colour) is the one external colour kept, used only on WhatsApp buttons, the floating WhatsApp button and WhatsApp-related status. It is not part of the Derico palette and should not be used for anything else.

### 1.5 Status colour mapping

| State | Colour | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| Success | `#16A34A` on a 10% green tint | Available, Confirmed, Paid, Delivered, Connected, Completed |
| Warning | `#F59E0B` on a 12% amber tint, dark amber text | Pending, Reserved, Limited, Licence expiring, Partially paid |
| Error | `#DC2626` on a 10% red tint | Failed, Overdue, Cancelled, Disconnected, Booked (unavailable dates) |
| Info / in progress | Royal Blue `#2563EB` on `#EFF6FF` | In progress, New request, Sent, Read |
| Neutral | Slate `#475569` on `#E8EDF4` | Sold, Draft, Archived, Inactive |

### 1.6 Other design decisions

| Item | Decision |
|---|---|
| Personality | Trustworthy, modern and approachable. A digital-first dealership. |
| Typography | Headings: a bold geometric sans (e.g. Poppins / Montserrat) in Navy. Body: Inter in Slate. Sizes: 14-16px body, 28-40px page titles. |
| Shape | 12px rounded cards, 8px rounded inputs and buttons, soft shadows |
| Imagery | Large car photos, 4:3 ratio cards, lazy-loaded, skeleton loaders |
| Icons | Lucide icon set |
| Layout | Mobile-first. Breakpoints: 360 / 768 / 1024 / 1280. Public site max width 1200px. Generous white space. |
| Dark mode | Not in this phase (keeps the palette consistent) |

### 1.7 Accessibility notes on the palette

- Body text `#475569` and headings `#14213D` on white pass AA contrast.
- **Muted Text `#8290A3` is low contrast on white** (about 3.3:1). Use it only for secondary or helper text, placeholders and disabled states, never for essential information or small body copy.
- **Warning Amber `#F59E0B` is not readable as text on white.** Use it as a badge or icon colour with dark amber text (for example `#92400E`) on an amber tint.
- Royal Blue buttons with white text pass AA. Always show a visible focus ring (`2px` Royal Blue, `2px` offset).
- Never rely on colour alone: pair status colours with an icon or label.
- Minimum 44px tap targets; labels on all inputs.

Performance mindset (Cameroon mobile data): light pages, compressed images, no heavy animations.

