## 9. WHATSAPP API in the design

WhatsApp appears in **five places**: public CTAs, booking/request drawers, the Messaging centre, automations and connection settings.

### 9.1 Public side
- Floating WhatsApp button, navbar button, CTA trio on every car, rental, pick-up and service page.
- Prefilled message text per page type (shown in a small "Preview message" tooltip in the prototype).
- Consent checkbox on every form: "I agree to receive confirmations and reminders on WhatsApp."

### 9.2 Message composer (reusable modal opened from any request, booking, invoice or driver)
- Recipient (name + number, editable).
- **Template picker** (dropdown): shows approved templates and their preview.
- Variable chips auto-filled from the record: `{{client_name}}`, `{{car}}`, `{{date}}`, `{{time}}`, `{{driver_name}}`, `{{driver_phone}}`, `{{amount}}`, `{{invoice_link}}`.
- **Free text** area: enabled only when the client messaged in the last 24 hours (show a countdown pill "Free text window: 3h 12m left"); otherwise greyed with tooltip "Outside 24-hour window: use a template."
- Attachments: invoice PDF, receipt PDF, car photo.
- Buttons: **Send now**, **Schedule**, **Send via WhatsApp app** (click-to-chat fallback, opens `wa.me` with the text prefilled).
- After send: message appears in the record's thread with status icons (clock = queued, one tick = sent, two ticks = delivered, blue two ticks = read, Error Red = failed with "Resend").

### 9.3 Messaging centre (admin)
**Tab 1: Inbox / Conversations**
- Two-pane layout: conversation list (client, last message, unread dot, linked booking tag) and chat view.
- Right info panel: client details, linked requests/bookings/invoices, quick actions (Create booking, Create invoice).
- Filters: Unread, Needs reply, Pending bookings, Failed.
- Note: shown as a design that works once the API (or provider) is connected; in fallback mode this tab shows "Inbox requires the WhatsApp API. Use Message log instead."

**Tab 2: Templates**
- Table: name, category (Utility, Marketing), language (EN/FR), status (Draft, Submitted, Approved, Rejected), last used.
- Create template: name, category, language, body with variable insertion, example values, live WhatsApp-style bubble preview, "Submit for approval" button, rejection reason display.
- Pre-seeded templates to show in the prototype: request received, viewing confirmation, viewing reminder, rental confirmed (with driver), rental handover reminder, return reminder, pick-up confirmed, pick-up reminder, driver assignment, booking cancelled, invoice sent, payment received, sales receipt.

**Tab 3: Automations**
- List of rules with on/off switches. Each rule: **Trigger** > **Delay/time** > **Template** > **Recipient**.
- Examples:
  | Trigger | Timing | Template | To |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | Request form submitted | Immediately | Request received | Client |
  | New request received | Immediately | New request alert | Admin |
  | Viewing scheduled | Immediately | Viewing confirmation | Client |
  | Viewing | 24h and 2h before | Viewing reminder | Client |
  | Rental confirmed | Immediately | Rental confirmed | Client |
  | Rental start / end | 24h before | Handover / return reminder | Client |
  | Pick-up confirmed | Immediately | Pick-up confirmed | Client and Driver |
  | Pick-up | 3h before | Pick-up reminder | Client and Driver |
  | Driver assigned | Immediately | Driver assignment | Driver |
  | Invoice overdue | Due date + 2 days | Payment reminder | Client |
- Rule editor: drawer with trigger dropdown, time offset control, template, recipients, quiet hours (e.g. do not send 21:00 to 07:00), language rule (client language or default).
- Toggle at top: "Automatic" vs "Manual approval first" (messages queue for admin to approve).

**Tab 4: Message log**
- Table: time, recipient, template, linked record, channel (WhatsApp API / Click-to-chat / SMS / Email), status, error. Filters by status and date. Row action: Resend. Export CSV.
- "Failed messages" banner with count and "Retry all".

### 9.4 Connection settings (Messaging > Connection)
A stepper-style page that supports the fallback plan:

1. **Status card:** Connected / Limited / Not connected, business number, display name, quality rating (High/Medium/Low shown as Success Green, Warning Amber, Error Red), daily usage meter (e.g. "84 of 250 unique contacts today"), verification badge status (Unverified / Verified).
2. **Connection method** (radio cards):
   - **A. Official WhatsApp API (Meta Cloud API)**: fields: Business account ID, Phone number ID, Access token, Webhook URL and verify token (with copy buttons), "Test connection" button.
   - **B. Through a provider (BSP)**: provider dropdown, API key, number.
   - **C. Click-to-chat mode (no registration)**: explains that the admin taps send; enables the "To send today" queue.
   - **D. Email / SMS backup**: SMTP and SMS provider fields.
3. **Verification checklist:** business name, registration certificate, tax number, proof of address, display name approved, two-factor enabled. Each item with a status chip and "Upload / Mark done".
4. **Fallback rules:** "If WhatsApp fails: retry 3 times, then send SMS/email, then alert admin."
5. **Opt-in and compliance:** consent text editor, list of clients who opted out.
6. **Test message:** send a test template to the admin number.

### 9.5 "To send today" queue (click-to-chat mode)
A dashboard card and a page listing messages due today (reminders, confirmations). Each row: recipient, message preview, **Open WhatsApp** button (wa.me link), **Mark as sent**. Counter shows remaining items.

